[lis@chaos.cs.brandeis.edu (Elisabeth Riba) writes:]
[] Here's a stupid question for you.  I've been playing for a while, and
[] want to know how to use missle weapons, i.e. bow & arrow, crossbow &
[] bolts, sling & rocks, etc.  If I try to wield the bow (for example) I

the protocol is that you wield the bow and then throw the arrow. this
arrangement makes the arrow more effective than merely tossing the
arrow without a bow in hand. similarly for crossbows/bolts, etc. the
problem is that missile weapons just aren't up to snuff (in my opinion),
shurikens and poisoned arrows being an exception. daggers and knives
are also preferred over arrows and rocks. given that you must waste a
move to wield a worthless weapon in order to get an effective missile
attack, the arrow strategy is currently typically not a win (there
being exceptional circumstances, of course). it would also be nice if
there were named bows that could make throwing arrows a serious threat.

